title: A slow chute onto a fast belt
intro: Conveyor cells can go at their own speeds: a slow chute drops crates onto a fast belt in the same line, changing speed at the join with no pause.

project: Empty | Chutes

chapter: The line | A chute at half a cell a second, a belt at three
create: Empty
rename: Line
add: Conveyor
set: Conveyor.Belts = 0 -3 down 0.5\n0 -2 down 0.5\n0 -1 down 0.5\n-3 0 right 3\n-2 0 right 3\n-1 0 right 3\n0 0 right 3\n1 0 right 3\n2 0 right 3\n3 0 right 3
explain: field:Conveyor.Belts | Belts | A number after a cell's way is its own speed in cells a second: the chute coming down column zero goes at half a cell a second, the belt along row zero at three.
set: Conveyor.Spacing = 0.25
set: Conveyor.MovingArrows = true
explain: field:Conveyor.MovingArrows | Moving Arrows | Each cell's arrows slide at its own speed, slow on the chute and fast on the belt.
look: 0, 1, 5

chapter: Machines | Boxes along the belt, crates down the chute, a bin at the end
deselect
create: Empty
rename: Boxes
set: Transform.Position.X = -4
add: Inventory
set: Inventory.Items = Box
editorset: Inventory.Items:count:1 = 8
add: ConveyorPort
set: ConveyorPort.Kind = Out
deselect
create: Empty
rename: Crates
set: Transform.Position = 0, 4, 0
add: Inventory
set: Inventory.Items = Crate
editorset: Inventory.Items:count:1 = 8
add: ConveyorPort
set: ConveyorPort.Kind = Out
explain: component:ConveyorPort | Conveyor Port | Crates go onto the top of the chute, boxes onto the start of the belt.
deselect
create: Empty
rename: Bin
set: Transform.Position.X = 4
add: ConveyorPort
explain: component:ConveyorPort | Conveyor Port | The bin at the belt's end takes everything.

chapter: Play | Slow down the chute, fast along the belt
play
wait: 4
say: Boxes race along the belt while crates creep down the chute, then speed up the moment they drop onto the belt, slotting in between the boxes.
wait: 10
expectvalue: Line.Conveyor.Count = 0
say: Everything reached the bin. From a script, SetRunSpeed sets a whole run's speed at once, and an Out port's Withdraw takes back an item it hasn't put on the belt yet.
stop
